      "curator_note": "adduct corrected to null: the precursor is an EVEN-ELECTRON cation (charge +1, radical_electrons 0), NOT the [M]+. radical molecular ion. (70 eV EI is retained as the book's standing condition under which such EE+ ions are formed, but the page prints no per-scheme ionization conditions.) Eq 4.21, EE+ (even-electron closed-shell cation) inductive cleavage R-Y+=CH2 -> R+ + Y=CH2. Page draws 1 double-barbed arc pulling the R-Y bonding pair onto the Y+ centre (heterolysis); the single encoded 2-electron move reproduces it. Instantiated as the methoxymethyl (oxocarbenium) cation CH3-O+=CH2 (Y=O, Y=CH2 -> formaldehyde)."
